# Reviewed allowlist for tests/test_san_report_sweep_2306.sh (#2306).
# Format: SECTION|PASS|row text|reason
# A row listed here still PASSES when the fake-sanitizer wrapper appends a
# UBSan "runtime error:" line to every program. Each entry needs a reason.
# The sweep fails if an entry goes stale, so remove it once its row is fixed.
[104]|PASS|cooperative tasks replay byte-identically (#408 determinism)|Semantic comparison of two captured outputs; this display row still passes the planted report. R31-6 adds separate Task pipeline first/second run completed checks, which consume both statuses and fail the hard diagnostic. The owning section therefore fails; this display row does not own completion.
[104]|PASS|virtual time is deterministic, replays, records zero nondet (#408 inc3)|Semantic comparison of three captured outputs; this display row still passes the planted report. R31-6 adds separate Virtual-time first/second/replay completed checks, which consume all three statuses and fail the hard diagnostic. The owning section therefore fails; this display row does not own completion.
[120]|PASS|'what is x at L' correct past line 65535 (111, 222)|A display sub-line of [120]'s single counted row (LW_OK). That row fails through its exit-status sub-line, which the sweep requires separately.
[120]|PASS|JIT tier agrees with interpreter past line 65535|A display sub-line of [120]'s single counted row. Same as above.
[120]|PASS|error line reported as 70005 (> 65535, not wrapped)|A display sub-line of [120]'s single counted row. Same as above.
[9/15]|PASS|AS1 assert true passes|Semantic output sub-row of test_assert.eigs. R31-6 adds the separate Assert program completed (status and final marker) consumer, which rejects the planted hard diagnostic. This value sub-row still matches its printed value while the owning section fails completion.
[9/15]|PASS|AS2 assert list passes|Same test_assert.eigs value-sub-row shape as AS1. Its separate Assert program completed consumer rejects the hard diagnostic; this printed-value match does not own program completion.
